{
  "_comment": [
    "Curated inputs for backend/scripts/import_landmarks.py. Edit by hand, then re-run the script.",
    "Keys under 'records' are '<source_name>:<source_record_id>'. Every field is optional:",
    "  include (bool)            keep a record whose source type is normally dropped (e.g. a famous stadium)",
    "  exclude (string)          drop the record; the string is the reason shown in the report",
    "  category                  force one of the 12 app categories",
    "  name                      replace the display name",
    "  geofence_radius_m         fixed radius (15..2000); wins over defaults and area-derived radii",
    "  espace_vert_index         attach the polygon of this NUM_INDEX from the 'Grands parcs, parcs",
    "                            d'arrondissements et espaces publics' dataset (or 'OBJECTID:<n>' for one feature)",
    "  osm_polygon               {name_regex, around_m}: look up a closed way / multipolygon relation in",
    "                            OpenStreetMap (Overpass) near the point; attached only if it contains the point",
    "  note                      free text, copied to the report (not to the database)",
    "'required' lists places that must be in the catalogue. If none of the imported records matches",
    "name_regex, the script tries OpenStreetMap (Overpass) and adds the place with needs_review = true."
  ],
